  "hypothesis": "Integrating A's aligned ring buffer and unrolled sliding-window max computation with B/C's fast scanner while removing OpenMP overhead from the inner loop yields lower runtime than prefix-sum based parallel scans.",
  "notes": "The candidate replaces per-row prefix-sum + OpenMP reduction with a single-threaded, unrolled sliding-window maximum over column sums. It also aligns both ring and column arrays to 64-byte boundaries using posix_memalign. This avoids thread creation/synchronization overhead for each vertical step while retaining the fast buffered scanner and 4-way unrolled I/O loops.",
